12	/// share sheet (research.md R2) via `SharePlatform.instance` directly —
13	/// `SharePlus.instance` caches its platform in a `static final` field on
14	/// first access, which would make it invisible to a test that reassigns
15	/// `SharePlatform.instance` afterward; going straight to the platform
16	/// interface (the same one `SharePlus`/`Share` ultimately delegate to)
17	/// avoids that. A user-cancelled share is reported by `share_plus` as a
18	/// normal, non-throwing `ShareResult` — never reaches the `catch` below,
19	/// and is treated as success: the file *was* produced and offered.
